% ============================================================
% Task 3: Belief Revision (Contradictory Evidence)
% Tests whether NARS correctly revises a prior belief when
% conflicting evidence is presented.
%
% Inference mode: Revision (NAL-1)
% Ground truth: revised belief should have intermediate f, moderate c
% ============================================================

% Prior belief: Tom is likely a cat (high confidence)
<tom --> cat>. %{0.90 0.90}

% Conflicting evidence: tom is probably NOT a cat
<tom --> cat>. %{0.10 0.80}

% Query: What is the current belief about tom being a cat?
<tom --> cat>?

% Expected: NARS revision formula:
%   f_rev = (f1*c1 + f2*c2) / (c1 + c2)
%         = (0.9*0.9 + 0.1*0.8) / (0.9 + 0.8)
%         = (0.81 + 0.08) / 1.7 = 0.524
%   c_rev = (c1 + c2) / (c1 + c2 + 1)
%         = 1.7 / 2.7 = 0.630
% Ground-truth: f* ~ 0.52, c* ~ 0.63
